{
  "duration": 72.479,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.059,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.559,
      "end": 2.839,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.319,
      "end": 6.779,
      "text": "In this problem, we are given that tan theta is equal to three by four,"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.259,
      "end": 9.539,
      "text": "and we need to find sine theta plus cos theta."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.019,
      "end": 11.239,
      "text": "What does this mean in simple words?"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.659,
      "end": 15.099,
      "text": "Tan theta tells us the ratio of opposite side to adjacent side."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.639,
      "end": 17.739,
      "text": "So if tan theta is equal to three by four,"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.239,
      "end": 23.519,
      "text": "we can imagine a right-angled triangle where the opposite side is three and the adjacent side is four."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.959,
      "end": 28.319,
      "text": "A three-four right triangle immediately reminds us of one famous triangle,"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.699,
      "end": 30.179,
      "text": "the three-four-five triangle."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.5,
      "end": 32.279,
      "text": "So the hypotenuse will be five."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.639,
      "end": 33.639,
      "text": "Got it? Perfect."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.439,
      "end": 39.84,
      "text": "Now that we know all three sides, finding sine theta and cos theta becomes very easy."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.36,
      "end": 43.84,
      "text": "Sine theta means opposite side divided by hypotenuse."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.239,
      "end": 50.279,
      "text": "So sine theta is equal to three by five, and cos theta means adjacent side divided by hypotenuse."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.639,
      "end": 52.879,
      "text": "So cos theta is equal to four by five."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.279,
      "end": 55.619,
      "text": "Now these values will help us find the required answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.099,
      "end": 60.639,
      "text": "We need sine theta plus cos theta, so three by five plus four by five."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.039,
      "end": 64.279,
      "text": "Since the denominators are the same, we simply add the numerators."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.699,
      "end": 66.099,
      "text": "This becomes seven by five."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.54,
      "end": 67.319,
      "text": "Done and dusted."
    },
    {
      "start": 68.119,
      "end": 72.479,
      "text": "Hence, the final answer will be seven by five. So the correct option is A."
    }
  ],
